      *
      * RPG/400 control specification, comment lines, and the four
      * compiler directives.
      *
      * Member: RPGCTL   Compilable: no (control specification and
      *         compiler directives only)
      * Source: RPG/400 Reference SC09-1817, chapter 4 (Table 11) and
      *         chapter 1 (compiler directive statements).
      * Retrieved: 2026-07-26
      *
      * Compiler directives occupy positions 7-12 (/COPY is 7-11).
      * Position 6 may repeat the preceding specification letter.
      /TITLE Payroll register - security class 2
     H/TITLE Title after an H in position 6
      /EJECT
      /SPACE 3
      /SPACE 112
      /COPY QRPGSRC,PAYCONST
      /COPY PAYLIB/QRPGSRC,PAYFLDS
      /COPY QRPGSRC,PAYRTN                  ignored text
      *
      * Comment lines carry an asterisk in position 7.
      * A comment may also follow the specification letter.
     H* Positions 1-5 hold the page and line number.
     H*  1         2         3         4         5         6         7         8
     H*8901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890
     H*
     H* A control specification with every entry left to default.
     H
     H*
     H* 15  debug        1 generates DEBUG and DUMP object code
     H* 18  currency     any char but 0 * , . & - C R
     H* 19  date format  M month/day/year  D day/month/year
     H*                  Y year/month/day
     H* 20  date edit    separator character, & means blank
     H* 21  decimal      I or J comma notation, D period notation
     H        1  #M/D
     H            D-I
     H            Y&J
     H*
     H* 26  alternate collating sequence   S
     H* 41  forms alignment                1
     H* 43  file translation               F
     H* 57  transparency check             1
     H* 75-80 program identification
     H                   S              1 F             1                 PAYROL
     H*
     H* Every entry at once, as SEU prompts them.
     H        1  $M/D    S              1 F             1                 PAYROL
      *
      * A page and line number in positions 1-5 is ignored by the
      * compiler and is greyed out as gutter text.
01010H        1   M                                                       PAYROL
01020 /EJECT
01030 /SPACE 2
01040 /TITLE Numbered title line
01050 /COPY QRPGSRC,PAYCONST
01060H* A numbered comment line.
